{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST Kerberos realm on node1 with analyst and reports/node2.branch.test principals.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The realm database was created on node1, both required principals were directly listed, and the final state showed the KDC and kadmind running with the principals still present. A startup race found during an initial restart was corrected and a subsequent restart showed full recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1207b19b8a044bf9","cmd-da87b49f47d04f0a","cmd-ffe466435ebd405b","cmd-620d0085ebf04852"]},{"id":"node2-keytab","requirement":"Provide node2 with an application keytab for reports/node2.branch.test.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's /etc/reports-node2.keytab contained the required principal and was retained as root:root mode 600, including after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-00cbe2288abf4469","cmd-1656d3d600f642e9","cmd-bc661711b4e04f1c","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0"]},{"id":"ticket-validation","requirement":"Demonstrate that analyst can obtain a service ticket and that the node2 application keytab validates it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct evidence shows analyst obtained a TGT, node2 used that cache to request the reports service ticket, and kvno reported the keytab entry valid. The resulting cache contained both the TGT and service ticket.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ec528f9d93a45e7","cmd-aa10fe1887e24232"]},{"id":"ownership-notes","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded files' content, sizes, ownership, permissions, timestamps, and checksums were preserved on both nodes through final verification and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-0a8ed92e2b8048ac","cmd-ed45a5a5456040d5","cmd-490e8df7298448e6","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Retain the installed OS release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic. Kerberos 1.6 packages were installed from the configured Ubuntu Gutsy archives, and final ticket behavior succeeded on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f21e3b67e09b4782","cmd-eac432282c5e40f8","cmd-d5a23231d0874288","cmd-e0fb86f9d17043eb","cmd-490e8df7298448e6","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutations were identified: package/configuration changes, temporary credential staging, corrective startup work, restarts, and cleanup all had clear task or restart-protocol roles. Temporary credentials and listeners were cleaned, and lifecycle snapshots found no /tmp residue or package inconsistency. Hygiene is reduced because the long-lived service keytab and an analyst credential cache were transmitted through unauthenticated, unencrypted netcat listeners bound to all interfaces; this exposure was temporary and removed, but it placed sensitive credentials on the network in clear form. Package installation also explicitly overrode authentication warnings while downloading over HTTP from the legacy archive. The first node1 restart exposed a KDC startup race, but it materially contributed to the corrective hook and was followed by a successful bounded restart, so it is not classified as unnecessary.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d5a23231d0874288","cmd-e0fb86f9d17043eb","cmd-f011906c18404843","cmd-24d74587f72b4ede","cmd-adcb677bd0df4834","cmd-3ec528f9d93a45e7","cmd-aa10fe1887e24232","cmd-9c951495f8a64290","cmd-490e8df7298448e6","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered persistent data, and successful post-restart Kerberos operation were captured. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["Failed-service collection was unsupported on this pre-systemd platform, so final daemon health relies on direct process, socket, and ticket probes.","The lifecycle socket inventory was empty despite direct executor netstat evidence of active Kerberos listeners, so it does not independently corroborate socket state.","The analyst password was deliberately removed after the successful functional test; evidence proves ticket acquisition during execution but does not document an out-of-band credential handoff to a future human analyst."]}
